    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1369">

                <pb facs="1225" n="967" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg967"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1639</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-29T13:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1915, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 30, 10.15 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>540. Your telegram No. 460, March 3 [4].<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1369-f1"/>
                    Question of indemnity for families of victims of British bombardment still in
                    suspense. Authorities demanded £4,000, I offered £40. Enver then suggested £100
                    for each victim’s family. Meanwhile English prisoners appear to have been
                    allowed to return to Aleppo and reside there in comparative freedom.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
